.TH NETWORK 1 "September 2025" "MyWallet Toolkit 2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
network \- Bitcoin network configuration management for toolkit commands
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B network.sh
.RB [ \-q ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-a
.IR action ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR config_file ]
.RB [ \-h ]
.RI [ network ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B network.sh
manages Bitcoin network selection for MyWallet Toolkit commands. It provides persistent configuration storage, network switching capabilities, and automatic detection for other tools in the suite.

The network configuration affects all toolkit commands that interact with Bitcoin networks, including balance checking, transaction sending, and address validation. The configuration is stored persistently and can be overridden by environment variables.

.B TESTED AND VERIFIED:
This component has been tested with network switching between mainnet and testnet, persistent configuration storage, and integration with other toolkit components.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-q
Quiet mode. Suppress informational output.
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose mode. Show detailed operations and configuration paths.
.TP
.B \-a \fIaction\fR
Action to perform:
.RS
.TP
.B show
Display current network setting (default)
.TP
.B set
Set network configuration (requires network argument)
.TP
.B status
Show network status and API connectivity
.RE
.TP
.B \-c \fIconfig_file\fR
Configuration file path (default: ~/.bitcoin-toolkit-config)
.TP
.B \-h
Show help message and exit.

.SH NETWORKS
.TP
.B mainnet
Bitcoin main network with real funds and transactions. Use with extreme caution.
.TP
.B testnet
Bitcoin test network for development and testing. Funds have no real value.

.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B show
Display the currently configured network. This is the default action when no action is specified.
.TP
.B set \fInetwork\fR
Set the network configuration to mainnet or testnet. The setting is saved persistently to the configuration file.
.TP
.B status
Show detailed network status including configuration source, API connectivity tests, and integration status.

.SH CONFIGURATION HIERARCHY
The network setting is determined by the following priority order:
.IP 1. 4
BITCOIN_NETWORK environment variable (highest priority)
.IP 2. 4
Configuration file setting
.IP 3. 4
Default value (mainnet) if no configuration exists

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Show current network:
.B network.sh
.br
or
.br
.B network.sh -a show
.TP
Switch to testnet:
.B network.sh -a set testnet
.TP
Switch to mainnet with verbose output:
.B network.sh -v -a set mainnet
.TP
Check network status:
.B network.sh -a status
.TP
Use custom configuration file:
.B network.sh -c /path/to/config -a set testnet
.TP
Override with environment variable:
.B BITCOIN_NETWORK=testnet balance.sh address

.SH CONFIGURATION FILE
The configuration is stored in a simple text file format:
.TP
.B Default Location
~/.bitcoin-toolkit-config
.TP
.B Format
The file contains a single line with the network name (mainnet or testnet).
.TP
.B Permissions
The file is created with secure permissions (600) to prevent unauthorized access.

.SH INTEGRATION
The network configuration integrates with other toolkit components:
.SS Automatic Detection
Other tools automatically detect the network setting:
.IP \(bu 4
.BR balance (1)
uses network for API endpoint selection
.IP \(bu 4
.BR send-secure (1)
uses network for transaction validation
.IP \(bu 4
.BR address (1)
uses network for address format validation

.SS Environment Override
The BITCOIN_NETWORK environment variable can override the configuration:
.nf
.B BITCOIN_NETWORK=testnet balance.sh address
.I # Temporarily use testnet regardless of config
.fi

.SH API INTEGRATION
Network configuration affects API endpoints:
.SS Mainnet APIs
.IP \(bu 4
https://blockstream.info/api/
.IP \(bu 4
https://api.blockcypher.com/v1/btc/main/

.SS Testnet APIs
.IP \(bu 4
https://blockstream.info/testnet/api/
.IP \(bu 4
https://api.blockcypher.com/v1/btc/test3/

