.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Operation completed successfully
.TP
.B 1
Invalid network specified, file system error, or invalid arguments

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BITCOIN_NETWORK
Override the configured network setting. Takes precedence over configuration file.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.bitcoin-toolkit-config
Default network configuration file. Contains the selected network (mainnet or testnet).

.SH SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
.IP \(bu 4
Configuration file created with secure permissions (600)
.IP \(bu 4
Network validation prevents invalid settings
.IP \(bu 4
No sensitive information stored in configuration
.IP \(bu 4
Environment variable support for temporary overrides

.SH INTEGRATION EXAMPLES
.TP
Set testnet globally for development:
.nf
.B network.sh -a set testnet
.B balance.sh tb1q...
.I # Uses testnet automatically
.fi
.TP
Temporary mainnet override:
.B BITCOIN_NETWORK=mainnet balance.sh 1A1z...
.TP
Pipeline with network awareness:
.nf
.B network.sh -a set testnet
.B echo private_key | public_key.sh | address.sh | balance.sh
.I # Entire pipeline uses testnet
.fi

